<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  WayBionic arm - "full-arm-smaller", mechanical drop of 2026-09-05.

  REBUILT FROM, NOT EQUAL TO, THE SUPPLIED EXPORT.
  sep_05_latest_info/full-arm-smaller.urdf could not be used as delivered:

    * Every one of its 12 links parented straight to the assembly root, so it
      described a star, not a chain. MoveIt has nothing to traverse in a star.
    * Its root link carried the WHOLE assembly as one mesh - 218740 triangles -
      while the same 218740 triangles were repeated across the 12 part meshes.
      Every surface was drawn twice and every pair of links was in permanent
      self-collision.
    * Its joints were exporter noise: 6 fixed, 5 prismatic pinned at
      lower=0 upper=0 effort=0 velocity=0, 1 unbounded continuous. No usable DOF.
    * Link, joint and mesh names contained spaces, which become tf frame names.
    * Worst of all, four of its six link frames sat at the ASSEMBLY ORIGIN,
      1.5-1.8 m away from the part they belonged to. The model renders
      correctly at the zero pose, so the fault is invisible until something
      moves - then each joint swings its child through a metre-plus arc.

  What was done: the root aggregate mesh was dropped, the 12 part meshes were
  re-parented into the serial chain below, and every link frame was moved onto
  its physical pivot with the visual/collision/inertial origins compensated so
  the rendered pose is unchanged. Dropping the aggregate is loss-free - the 12
  parts, placed by their original transforms, reproduce the root mesh bounding
  box to 5.7e-05 m, and this file reproduces the export's rendered pose at the
  zero configuration to within 1.3e-05 m.

  WHAT IS MEASURED vs WHAT IS ASSUMED
  ===================================
  MEASURED - taken unchanged from the export, trustworthy:
    - every link's mesh, colour and inertial block
    - each link's POSE relative to the assembly root, given exactly by the
      export, which makes the re-parenting arithmetic exact:
      T_parent->child = T_root->parent^-1 . T_root->child
    - the axes of joint2..joint5, from the CAD Axis_* coordinate systems

  ASSUMED - INTERIM, UNVERIFIED, pending mechanical:
    - THE CHAIN ORDER ITSELF. Inferred from measured height up the assembly
      and from the CSV "SW Components" column. Mechanical has not stated which
      part drives which. If the order is wrong, so is every reachability and
      collision result computed from this file.
    - joint1's axis. No Axis_Sweep exists in the export; the world vertical is
      used, which is what a base yaw turns about.
    - EVERY JOINT'S PIVOT LOCATION. The export supplies an axis DIRECTION for
      some joints but never a point on it, so each pivot is estimated as the
      midpoint of the closest approach between the parent's and the child's
      geometry - where the two parts physically meet. Measured interface gaps
      were 0.0001-0.067 m, so the parts do touch there, but the exact pivot is
      mechanical's to confirm.
    - EVERY LIMIT. +/-1.5708 rad (+/-90 deg) is a deliberately conservative
      placeholder, not a measurement, chosen to match the convention the
      retired full_arm_mar24.urdf used. effort/velocity likewise.
    - which structural link each fastener/drive part bolts to (see below).

  KNOWN DEGENERACY - THE ARM CANNOT CHANGE ITS TIP HEIGHT
  ======================================================
  All five axes below come out within 1.6 degrees of vertical, and joint3,
  joint4 and joint5 are mutually coaxial. That is not a modelling slip, it is
  what the export contains: the only parts carrying a CAD Axis_* frame are
  3rd joint bend, diff-assembly-pulley and biomed lock mech, which are the
  three bodies of the tool column, all spinning about that column. The export
  contains NO shoulder or elbow BEND axis anywhere - the CSV never defines one.

  Consequence, measured over 200000 sampled configurations: the tool tip
  sweeps a 0.51 m x 0.56 m PLANE at z = 0.695 m, with 6.8 mm of total vertical
  travel. The arm is a SCARA, not a 5-DOF arm. Anything needing a change of
  height - including the Z leg of scripts/ik_xyz_demo.py, which steps 40 mm -
  has no solution and never will until mechanical supplies the bend axes.

  Fixing this needs data, not modelling: ask mechanical for the rotation axis
  of each joint, as a SolidWorks reference axis on the part that rotates.

  Until mechanical confirms the above, do NOT read the RViz workspace as a
  statement of what this arm can actually reach.
-->
<robot name="full-arm-smaller">

  <!-- Dummy root so KDL does not discard base_link's inertia. -->
  <link name="world"/>
  <joint name="world_to_base" type="fixed">
    <parent link="world"/>
    <child link="base_link"/>
    <!-- The STL vertices keep their original SolidWorks assembly coordinates.
         This centres the assembly on the world origin in XY and drops its
         lowest point onto the z=0 ground plane. -->
    <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="base_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.052227 0.0604364 0.0293091" rpy="1.5708 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.2997"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.0036992" ixy="-4.7879E-13" ixz="3.5114E-10" iyy="0.007244" iyz="-1.5577E-05" izz="0.0037785"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.664103 1.42744 -0.903496" rpy="1.5708 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/bottom_base_assembly.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <collision name="base_link_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.0522358 0.0594201 0.029995" rpy="1.5708 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1998 0.0600 0.2000"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <!-- INTERIM LIMITS AND INTERIM TOPOLOGY - UNVERIFIED. Mechanical supplied no
       travel, effort or velocity figures, and no parent/child relationships at
       all. +/-1.5708 rad is a conservative placeholder, NOT a measurement; the
       identical effort/velocity values below are placeholders too - no real
       mechanism has five joints with matching dynamics. Replace all of these,
       and re-check the chain order, once mechanical confirms real values. -->
  <link name="sweep">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.0163929 0.0756448 -0.160886" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.26997"/>
      <inertia ixx="6.5782E-05" ixy="1.1446E-05" ixz="-2.7313E-09" iyy="8.2674E-05" iyz="-2.7407E-09" izz="8.8451E-05"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.653777 -0.859305 -1.32289" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/sweep.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <collision name="sweep_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.0148926 0.0721225 -0.169349" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.0738 0.1785 0.2713"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <!-- joint1: base yaw. Driven by the sweep gearbox; axis derived from the world
       vertical because the export defines no Axis_Sweep. -->
  <joint name="joint1" type="revolute">
    <origin xyz="0.0538204 0.0844065 0.0936804" rpy="-3.14159 0 -1.0472"/>
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="sweep"/>
    <axis xyz="0 -7.34641e-06 -1"/>
    <limit lower="-1.5708" upper="1.5708" effort="10" velocity="1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="shoulder">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.00833119 0.0644138 0.0215281" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.19918"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00044506" ixy="0.00011586" ixz="-4.3871E-08" iyy="0.00034473" iyz="-4.7682E-08" izz="0.00051429"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.824841 -0.818826 -1.32207" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/shouldersplit.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <collision name="shoulder_collision">
      <origin xyz="-0.00976251 0.072516 0.0215282" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1224 0.1325 0.0800"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <!-- joint2: shoulder. Axis is the nema23 motor axis - the CSV lists that motor's
       components as nema23_w_shoulder / j2_nema23_gearbox. -->
  <joint name="joint2" type="revolute">
    <origin xyz="0.00732929 0.162696 -0.255115" rpy="-3.14158 1.1744 2.6739"/>
    <parent link="sweep"/>
    <child link="shoulder"/>
    <axis xyz="0.92246 0 0.386093"/>
    <limit lower="-1.5708" upper="1.5708" effort="10" velocity="1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="elbow">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.0652637 0.0704856 -0.00263955" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.17976"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00030235" ixy="-7.4527E-05" ixz="-9.963E-10" iyy="0.00037544" iyz="-5.4808E-10" izz="0.00040872"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.00249731 0.0319966 -0.0026393" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/third_joint_bend.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="1 1 1 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <collision name="elbow_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.0641974 0.0727466 -0.0026393" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1365 0.1135 0.0900"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <!-- joint3: elbow bend. Axis from the CAD Axis_3rd joint bend frame. -->
  <joint name="joint3" type="revolute">
    <origin xyz="-0.0248502 -0.0097306 0.00472633" rpy="3.14159 -0.3685 0"/>
    <parent link="shoulder"/>
    <child link="elbow"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
    <limit lower="-1.5708" upper="1.5708" effort="10" velocity="1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="forearm">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.000881305 0.114186 -0.0412555" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.86499"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00088427" ixy="3.205E-05" ixz="-3.2838E-07" iyy="0.00094021" iyz="-2.3104E-07" izz="0.0010963"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.684809 -0.00415398 -1.36196" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/diff_assembly_pulley.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <collision name="forearm_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.000885343 0.117867 -0.0412673" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1274 0.2477 0.0953"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <!-- joint4: differential/forearm roll. Axis from Axis_diff-assembly-pulley. -->
  <joint name="joint4" type="revolute">
    <origin xyz="0.126943 0.0836319 -0.0439034" rpy="-3.14159 -3.3663e-05 1.5708"/>
    <parent link="elbow"/>
    <child link="forearm"/>
    <axis xyz="0 1 0"/>
    <limit lower="-1.5708" upper="1.5708" effort="10" velocity="1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="tool">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.0261854 -0.00183018 0.0147985" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.053298"/>
      <inertia ixx="1.3634E-05" ixy="-8.735E-22" ixz="-1.8806E-08" iyy="1.8285E-05" iyz="1.1597E-07" izz="1.3317E-05"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.0256756 -0.0265892 0.0148688" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/biomed_lock_mech.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <collision name="tool_collision">
      <origin xyz="-0.0261702 -0.00899661 0.014685" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.0599 0.0381 0.0599"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <!-- joint5: tool lock. Axis from Axis_biomed lock mech. -->
  <joint name="joint5" type="revolute">
    <origin xyz="0.0251063 0.240781 -0.0220181" rpy="0.0529983 -1.16738 -0.0487647"/>
    <parent link="forearm"/>
    <child link="tool"/>
    <axis xyz="0.0191131 -0.999784 0.00814643"/>
    <limit lower="-1.5708" upper="1.5708" effort="10" velocity="1.0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ===== Non-structural parts =====
       Drive and fastener geometry, carried so the arm still renders complete.
       No collision volume and no DOF: they are cosmetic here.
       Each is bolted to the structural link whose placed centroid is nearest.
       CAVEAT: m3 and heat_set_insert are MULTI-INSTANCE meshes - one mesh holds
       every screw and insert in the assembly, including ones that physically
       belong to distal links. They ride the sweep link, so they will not track
       the arm correctly once the distal joints move. Ask mechanical to export
       fasteners per-link, or to omit them. -->
  <link name="stepper">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.64313 0.8998 1.2835" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.45705"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00037382" ixy="1.0743E-07" ixz="9.7233E-06" iyy="0.0005475" iyz="2.5993E-07" izz="0.00038353"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/stepper.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="stepper_mount" type="fixed">
    <origin xyz="-0.0631287 1.48217 0.83867" rpy="-1.57079 -3.67317e-06 -2.618"/>
    <parent link="sweep"/>
    <child link="stepper"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="nema23">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.10166 0.070102 0.0018368" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.0827"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.0014882" ixy="-0.00023608" ixz="-5.2655E-05" iyy="0.0014342" iyz="-4.7983E-05" izz="0.0015666"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/nema23.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="nema23_mount" type="fixed">
    <origin xyz="0.0208635 0.0138745 -0.0531229" rpy="-1.5708 6.55747e-06 1.1031"/>
    <parent link="sweep"/>
    <child link="nema23"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="outerring">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.0080961 0.027364 -0.026357" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.29137"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.00023769" ixy="1.4814E-05" ixz="1.3088E-12" iyy="0.00026688" iyz="-1.3596E-12" izz="0.00036814"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/outerring.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.79216 0.81961 0.93333 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="outerring_mount" type="fixed">
    <origin xyz="0.0727054 0.116482 -0.121794" rpy="-1.5708 0.396367 -0.467733"/>
    <parent link="sweep"/>
    <child link="outerring"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="heat_set_insert">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.02981 -0.0047361 0.051895" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.00011545"/>
      <inertia ixx="3.5199E-10" ixy="6.9974E-13" ixz="-5.5737E-14" iyy="3.5037E-10" iyz="-2.0825E-14" izz="3.5866E-10"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/heat_set_insert.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.79216 0.81961 0.93333 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="heat_set_insert_mount" type="fixed">
    <origin xyz="0.0555045 0.0338746 -0.024123" rpy="-3.14159 8.0726e-07 3.03149"/>
    <parent link="sweep"/>
    <child link="heat_set_insert"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="m3">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.060837 -0.13261 -0.0085639" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.00029834"/>
      <inertia ixx="1.068E-08" ixy="-2.7807E-09" ixz="-8.3275E-11" iyy="4.0957E-09" iyz="-2.2672E-10" izz="9.2816E-09"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/m3.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="0.75294 0.75294 0.75294 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="m3_mount" type="fixed">
    <origin xyz="0.0174887 0.0609183 -0.275093" rpy="-1.60049 0.350493 -2.0487"/>
    <parent link="sweep"/>
    <child link="m3"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="bevel_gear">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.023575 -0.00015203 0.00068011" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.042026"/>
      <inertia ixx="9.9802E-06" ixy="-4.8977E-09" ixz="4.0392E-09" iyy="5.3605E-06" iyz="-8.7432E-07" izz="6.9939E-06"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://waybionic_description/meshes/bevel_gear.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="">
        <color rgba="1 0.94902 0.9098 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="bevel_gear_mount" type="fixed">
    <origin xyz="-0.0255987 -0.0506903 0.0148612" rpy="1.57081 1.3833e-05 -1.57079"/>
    <parent link="tool"/>
    <child link="bevel_gear"/>
  </joint>

</robot>
